# Moxa ioLogik E1241.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Moxa ioLogik E1241 Remote Ethernet I/O — 4-channel AO
# | 
# | Source: ioLogik E1200 Series User Manual V16.2, August 2025 (Appendix A)
# | Protocol: Modbus/TCP (port 502); Modbus/TCP ID default = 1
# | 
# | AO channels (ch0-3):
# | FC01 addr 4128-4131: AO_p2pSafeModeFlagClear ch0-3 (1=clear safe mode flag; R/W)
# | FC02 addr 4096-4099: AO_p2pStatus ch0-3 (R)
# | FC02 addr 4112-4115: AO_p2pSafeModeFlag ch0-3 (R)
# | FC01 addr 4144: watchdogAlarmFlag (R/W)
# | System FC04: same as other E1200 models
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Moxa
@model=ioLogik E1241
@description=4-AO remote Ethernet I/O, Modbus/TCP. FC03: AO_scaledValue u32 hi/lo ch0-3 (addr 0-7 R/W), AO_rawValue ch0-3 (addr 1024-1027 R/W). FC02: AO_p2pStatus (4096-4099), AO_p2pSafeModeFlag (4112-4115). FC01: AO_p2pSafeModeFlagClear (4128-4131), watchdogAlarmFlag (4144).
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/moxa-iologik-e1241.toml; Source: ioLogik E1200 Series User Manual V16.2, August 2025 (Appendix A). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
@byte_order=ABCD
@address_base=0
@x_status=unverified
